<!--
  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

  The simulated PSTN trunk.

  An IP trunk in both directions: we never register and the peer never
  challenges us, so the gateway exists only to name a destination address for
  outbound INVITEs. Inbound calls from the same peer arrive on the external
  profile, which already runs with auth-calls disabled, and land in the public
  context named below - the same context the profile itself would have given
  them, stated explicitly so gateway matching cannot move them elsewhere.

  caller-id-in-from is what makes the trunk transparent: without it every
  outbound call would announce itself as the gateway's own username, and the
  number the caller actually dialled from would never reach the peer.

  No ping: an OPTIONS keepalive would mark the gateway down whenever the
  simulator declines to answer it, and a gateway marked down rejects calls it
  could otherwise have placed. A NOREG gateway is dialable as it stands.

  outbound-proxy is what keeps an established call hanging together. The peer
  advertises a public address in the Via and Contact of its answers rather than
  the LAN address it actually occupies, and a Contact is where in-dialog
  requests are sent. Left alone, our ACK and our BYE both go to that public
  address and arrive nowhere: the peer tears the call down with
  Reason: SIP;cause=408 "ACK Timeout" because the ACK never came, then
  retransmits its own BYE ten times over thirty-two seconds because our 200 is
  going to the same dead address. The caller sits through all of it.

  Naming the proxy here pins the dialog's route set to the address the peer is
  really at, so ACK and BYE follow the same path the INVITE did. It fixes the
  teardown rather than papering over it with a media timeout.
-->
<include>
  <gateway name="pstn_gateway">
    <param name="proxy" value="$${pstn_gateway_host}:$${pstn_gateway_port}"/>
    <param name="outbound-proxy" value="$${pstn_gateway_host}:$${pstn_gateway_port}"/>
    <param name="register" value="false"/>
    <param name="caller-id-in-from" value="true"/>
    <param name="context" value="public"/>
  </gateway>
</include>
